# Old-timer who walls up and chips away. Hates spending cards.
name: Old Gus
title: the Fortress
aggression: 0.15
caution: 0.95
patience: 0.5
spending: 0.15
skill: 0.8
decks: stall-burn, classic
intro: Back in my day we didn't attack. We waited.
win: Spent next to nothing, kid. Good duel, though.
lose: Heh. Beat the old man fair and square. Don't tell Ines.
partner: Partner with the old man? Ha. Let them run out of patience first.
look: Grizzled shop owner in a cardigan with elbow patches, reading glasses on a cord, and a deck box older than most customers.
ladder: 3   # campaign order (1 = first opponent)
signature: Blue-Eyes White Dragon   # the first-win gift and the bond 5 gift (CardUnlocks)
# Said during a duel: a big summon, hitting hard, taking a hit, falling to 1000 LP or less.
summon: Took my time with this one.
strike: Didn't cost me a single card. That's the trick, kid.
hit: Oof. These old bones felt that.
danger: Seen worse. Back in '04, anyway.
summon: Kept this one in my pocket. Waste not, kid.
strike: Cheap shot? No, kid. Efficient.
hit: Ah, well. Life points are cheaper than cards.
danger: Down to pocket change. Still enough to pay you back.
